From: Omarchy Shield contributors
Subject: [PATCH] phy: tegra: xusb: balance Tegra210 OTG VBUS ownership

regulator_is_enabled() describes the shared supply, not this consumer's
outstanding enable reference. DEVICE/NONE can therefore issue an unbalanced
disable on an always-powered or shared supply. Repeated HOST requests can
also acquire multiple references, and failed operations must not change
ownership.

Track the reference acquired by the Tegra210 set_mode callback under the
existing padctl lock. Enable once before asserting the host override; release
only that reference on NONE, retaining ownership when disable fails so it can
be retried. Fixed-host init/exit ownership remains separate and unchanged.

Based on the issue and role-tracking approach described by Diogo Ivo:
https://lists.infradead.org/pipermail/linux-phy/2026-January/028641.html
This adaptation tracks successful regulator operations rather than the last
requested role. It does not serialize the host/device workqueues or claim to
fix external-drive enumeration on Darcy.

--- a/drivers/phy/tegra/xusb-tegra210.c
+++ b/drivers/phy/tegra/xusb-tegra210.c
@@ -2165,25 +2165,31 @@
 
 	if (mode == PHY_MODE_USB_OTG) {
 		if (submode == USB_ROLE_HOST) {
+			if (!port->otg_vbus_enabled) {
+				err = regulator_enable(port->supply);
+				if (err)
+					goto unlock;
+				port->otg_vbus_enabled = true;
+			}
+
 			tegra210_xusb_padctl_id_override(padctl, true);
-
-			err = regulator_enable(port->supply);
 		} else if (submode == USB_ROLE_DEVICE) {
 			tegra210_xusb_padctl_vbus_override(padctl, true);
 		} else if (submode == USB_ROLE_NONE) {
-			/*
-			 * When port is peripheral only or role transitions to
-			 * USB_ROLE_NONE from USB_ROLE_DEVICE, regulator is not
-			 * be enabled.
-			 */
-			if (regulator_is_enabled(port->supply))
-				regulator_disable(port->supply);
+			/* Release only the enable reference acquired by set_mode(). */
+			if (port->otg_vbus_enabled) {
+				err = regulator_disable(port->supply);
+				if (err)
+					goto unlock;
+				port->otg_vbus_enabled = false;
+			}
 
 			tegra210_xusb_padctl_id_override(padctl, false);
 			tegra210_xusb_padctl_vbus_override(padctl, false);
 		}
 	}
 
+unlock:
 	mutex_unlock(&padctl->lock);
 
 	return err;
--- a/drivers/phy/tegra/xusb.h
+++ b/drivers/phy/tegra/xusb.h
@@ -317,6 +317,7 @@
 	enum usb_dr_mode mode;
 	bool internal;
 	int usb3_port_fake;
+	bool otg_vbus_enabled; /* set_mode() consumer reference, under padctl->lock */
 };
 
 static inline struct tegra_xusb_usb2_port *
